prop vinewall14441 on.use=hide|
show|vinechest14441
message||The machete bites through the vines. Something was hidden behind them.
call ar_plants_snowy x=-56 z=-56 r=14 seed=14421
call ar_plants_snowy x=48 z=8 r=14 seed=14431

# --- Tools in use (10-24: a tool given earlier in the storyline is used again here, for optional finds): the
# machete from Triangulation Rocks cuts the vines over a hidden chest, and a zipline from the ridge top is the quick way back down
clear from 15.4 55.0 to 12 32 r=2.5
place ZiplinePath_Landmark ridgezip at 16 59 ground
zipto ridgezip 12 32

# --- Unique layer (10-24): stormworks device - see SL14_progress.md UNIQUE ISLANDS
call lever x=-51 z=6 yaw=180 al=cellarlever
prop cellarlever if.use=!signal|cellarbolt
prop cellarlever else.use=message||The lever is down. Far off, the cellar bolt is drawn.
prop cellarlever on.use=message||The lever drops with a bang. A rod rattles away through the hill - toward the smelthouse in the south.\nsignal||cellarbolt\ngive||story:cellarpin*1
call hatchcache x=13 z=-68.5 r=3 seed=14771 alias=cellarhatch chest=cellarchest items=TitaniumOre*3;MetalIngot*4;Battery*1
prop cellarchest note.title=Storm cellar
prop cellarhatch if.use=signal|cellarbolt
prop cellarhatch else.use=message||The cellar hatch is bolted from below. The smelters' roll says the bolt is drawn from the ore cave.
story cellarpin|Cellar bolt drawn|MetalIngot|The storm cellar's bolt is drawn: the lever by the ore cave dropped it.
prop orecavechest if.open=has|story:raft-Tangaroa_KeyCard|1
prop orecavechest else.open=message||The ore chest has a card slot stamped CONCORD. A keycard would open it.
loot orecavechest MetalOre*4;CopperOre*3;Bolt*2;TitaniumOre*3

# --- Deep (10-24, SL14 DEEP 1-HOUR PASS): the climb - a 36 m scaffold tower on its pad beside a raised peak, a plank
# bridge from landing 3 to the summit, the top locker, a stash on landing 2, a cairn and buried tin on the peak; the
# dive - a flooded pit with a wreck, an air bell, a chest and a sunk secret, a ramp out (lib_deep14)
call dp_ground tx=-25 tz=-70 hb=4.6 sx=-29.37 sz=-82.24 hs=26.2
call dp_tower ox=-26.36 oz=-67.12 hb=4.6 yaw=109.65 al=swtower top=swtop stash=swstash zal=swtopzone zid=sw_top msg="The top of the chimney scaffold. Smoke rolls past; the whole works under you."
call tzone x=-28.19 z=-78.94 al=swsummit id=sw_summit r=4 msg="The slag peak beside the chimney." h=1
call notebox x=-26.07 z=-83.42 yaw=199.65 al=swcairn
call treasure x=-31.25 z=-81.57 r=1.5 n=1 seed=14961
prop treasure14961 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;Battery*1
place ZiplinePath_Landmark swzip at -24.09 -71.92 h=40.6
zipto swzip -9.86 -27.62
place Creature_Goat swgoats at -16.32 -63.54 ground
prop swgoats creature.count=2
call dp_sink x=-58 z=50 d=-18 ex1=-49.67 ez1=42.82 ex2=-43.61 ez2=37.59 eh=2.55
place Van_1 swwreck at -58 50 ground sit yaw=40.76
place Loot_Chest swdivechest at -55.78 52.58 ground sit yaw=130.76
call dp_air x=-60.22 z=47.42 id=sw_air al=swair msg="Air trapped under the wreck - breathe."
place Loot_ChestSmall swdivesecret at -61.79 53.26 ground sit yaw=40.76
call tzone x=-58 z=50 al=swdivezone id=sw_dive r=7 msg="The bottom of the quench pool. A foundry van lies in the black water." h=1
call tzone x=-43.61 z=37.59 al=swrim id=sw_rim r=5 msg="The quench pool's rim." h=1
call treasure x=-40.58 z=34.98 r=2 n=1 seed=14962
prop treasure14962 treasure.loot=MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;Bolt*2
call dp_hazard x=-56 z=17 al=sw_dark kind=dark r=4 dmg=1 msg="Pitch dark in the ore cave - a headlight would help." y=1

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Stormworks
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A dark rock with smoke over it: the iron smelter hall where the Concord Engine's parts were cast, a weather room on its roof, a lightning rod on the spur - and the last crew's three notes.
island on.arrive=message||Smoke over a dark rock, and the smell of a forge. Up on the flat top, an iron hall with a dish on its roof.

note worksnote1 Stormworks note 1 | STORMWORKS - NOTE 1, painted on the hall wall in letters a metre high\n\nWhat the engine is for.\n\nThe sea rose and would not stop. The Concord was every station that agreed to try: the beacon, the intake, the relays, the wall, the locks, these works. We cast the rings here. The ring turns the sea - surface, deep and ice - so it stops rising.\n\nIt worked. That is the trouble. It never stops working.\n\nUnder it, in chalk, Hedda's capitals: SOMEONE HAS RELIT FURNACE 3. THE ASH IS WARM. - H.B.
note worksnote2 Stormworks note 2 | STORMWORKS - NOTE 2, the standing order to the last crew\n\nKeep the engine on standby. Do not shut it down - nobody knows what the sea does if the ring stops. Do not run it full - nobody knows that either. Station 1 has the switch. Station 1 decides.\n\nThe drone will keep the ring clean. Do not fight the drone. Do not feed the drone. Do not name the drone.\n\nPencilled under it: Somebody named the drone. It answers to Biscuit now. Please stop.\n\nWe went home anyway.
note worksnote3 Stormworks note 3 | STORMWORKS - NOTE 3, scratched into the rod's foot\n\nThe rafts call it the Stalker. It is not a beast.\n\nIt was our maintenance drone. It kept the ring clean of anything that grew on it, or swam into it, or came too close. When the crews left nobody told it to stop. It is still cleaning. It thinks you are something growing on the ring.\n\nBelow, fresh, in Hedda's hand: Saw one of them tonight, out over the south water, a long grey shape following an old man in a dory like a dog on a lead. He stopped, and it stopped. He went on, and it went on. It is not cleaning any more. It is guarding him.\n\nSouth, the pale tower in the steam. Ines is there. I am going to her. - H.
note hallchest Smelter hall | The hall's tool chest: an electric smelter's plans, soot in every fold.
note weatherchest Weather room | The weather room's chest: an advanced extractor's plans and a stopped barometer.
note anchorstore Anchor store | The anchor store on the clay beach: an advanced anchor's plans, for the ore barges.
note orebin1 Copper bin | An ore bin, half full of copper.
note orebin2 Iron bin | An ore bin, half full of iron.
loot hallchest Blueprint_SmelterElectric*1;MetalIngot*2;Scrap*4
prop hallchest loot.refill=0
loot weatherchest Blueprint_BiofuelExtractorAdvanced*1;Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1
prop weatherchest loot.refill=0
loot anchorstore Blueprint_AnchorStationaryAdvanced*1;Rope*6;MetalIngot*2
prop anchorstore loot.refill=0
loot orebin1 CopperOre*4
loot orebin2 MetalOre*4

note oreheap Furnace hands' store | The furnace hands' store: ore they never got to smelt.
loot oreheap MetalOre*4;CopperOre*3;TitaniumIngot*1;Plank*4
note furnaceletter Furnace hand's letter | A letter, never sent, folded small\n\nDear Ma,\n\nThe works make the iron for the great machine in the middle of the sea. They say when it is finished there will be no more storms.\n\nWe have made iron for eleven years. The storms are worse. The food is the same. The foreman says the storms are the sea arguing, and the Engine will win the argument. I said, Ma would win the argument, and he laughed so hard he burnt his hand.\n\nI miss your bread. I miss the rain that falls down. Here it goes sideways.\n\nYour son, Piet
note orecavechest Ore cave chest | A drill crew's chest: spare bits, a lamp wick, and ore they never carried out.
prop orecavechest loot.refill=0
note smeltroll Smelters' roll | SMELTERS' ROLL - pinned under a stone by the fallen wall\n\nShift 1 to 12, all present. Ore to the furnace, ingots to the pier. The ingots went south on the Concord's barges - every one stamped with the same ring.\n\nThe works closed the day the barges stopped coming. We melted the Concord's own ships in here, one by one, to feed the Engine; at the end we melted the last barge to make the bell clapper for the Well, and walked home round the coast.\n\nAdded at the bottom, careful and old: Shift 13. One man. Furnace 3 lit for one night, to cast a pin the Well door wants. Apologies for the mess. - S.W.
note oreplanelog Ore plane log | ORE PLANE LOG\n\nThe last load: ingots for the Engine, as the Concord ordered. The lightning followed us off the island - it struck the left wing twice, which the manual says cannot happen. I will write to the manual.\n\nDown in the east snow. The ingots are in the crate if anybody still wants them. The smelthouse hands keep their best ingots in the storm cellar, under the hatch, because they trust the cellar more than the foreman.
# (deep pass 10-24: the climb and the dive)
story mould|Bell mould|MetalIngot|An iron casting mould from the quench pool - the shape of the Engine's great bell clapper. The chimney locker is cut to take it.
note swdivechest Quench van | In the van's crate: an iron casting mould.
loot swdivechest story:mould*1;Rope*2;Scrap*3;MetalIngot*1
prop swdivechest loot.refill=0
note swtop Chimney locker | The mould sits in its cradle: the smelters' best ingots.
loot swtop TitaniumOre*3;Battery*1;Bolt*4
prop swtop loot.refill=0
prop swtop obj.name=swtop
prop swtop if.open=has|story:mould|1
prop swtop else.open=message||The chimney locker. An empty cradle in the lid, shaped for a casting mould.
note swstash Chimney stash | A smelter's bag, soot on everything.
loot swstash Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1;Nail*6
prop swstash loot.refill=0
note swdivesecret Quench strongbox | The smelters' wages, never paid.
loot swdivesecret MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*1
prop swdivesecret loot.refill=0
note swcairn Smoke cairn | A cairn on the slag peak:\n\nWe smelted ships to make the Engine. Every ingot has a name. - the crew
note keepersw Keeper's log: Stormworks | KEEPER'S LOG. The Stormworks, written in soot on the back of a shift card:\n\nFurnace 3 took a night to wake and two days to forgive me. I cast the pin the Well door wants; the old one rusted in the lock the year they sealed you in.\n\nThe drone found me here. It came up out of the quench pool dripping, all its lamps on, and I thought: this is how it ends, love, cleaned off the ring like a barnacle. It looked at me a long time. Then it followed me to the boat. It follows me still. I think it knows who I am waiting for. I think it waits for her too.\n\nThe captain is here, the hard one. She saw the drone. Good. Let her be afraid of it and not of me.\n\nCalling. Calling.\n\n- Silas
quest title=The Works
quest intro=A smelter hall under smoke on a dark rock. Go up to the hall.
step reach|smelter_hall|1|Go up to the smelter hall
step read|Stormworks note 1|1|Read the first note in the hall
step blueprint|Blueprint_SmelterElectric|1|Take the electric smelter plans from the hall's tool chest
step reach|weather_room|1|Climb up to the weather room on the roof
step read|Stormworks note 2|1|Read the second note in the weather room
step blueprint|Blueprint_BiofuelExtractorAdvanced|1|Take the advanced extractor plans from the weather room
step kill|Screecher|3|Drive the screechers off the rod spur
step blueprint|Blueprint_AnchorStationaryAdvanced|1|Take the advanced anchor plans from the store on the clay beach
step reach|stormridge|1|Climb the north ridge and watch the lightning
step read|Smelters' roll|1|Read the smelters' roll at the ruined smelthouse in the south
step collect|story:cellarpin|1|Drop the cellar lever by the ore cave in the west hills
step open|Storm cellar|1|Open the storm cellar under the hatch by the smelthouse
step reach|rod_top|1|Climb to the top of the rod spur
step read|Stormworks note 3|1|Read the last note under the lightning rod
quest done=The Stalker was the engine's drone, still cleaning. South, a pale tower stands in cold steam.
quest reward=MetalIngot*4;CopperOre*2;Scrap*6

save Stormworks
